.\" $Id$
.Dd $Mdocdate: June 3 2026$
.Dt PKGCTL 1
.Os BSD Mobile
.Sh NAME
Nm pkgctl
.Nd BSD-based package manager for mobile OS
.Sh SYNOPSIS
Nm pkgctl
.Op Fl h
.Op Fl v
.Op Ar command [ Ar arguments ]
.Sh DESCRIPTION
pkgctl is a command-line interface for managing packages on a BSD-derived mobile operating system.
It provides functions to install, remove, query, and update packages and repositories.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width install
.It Ar install Ar package
Install a package from the configured repositories.
.It Ar remove Ar package
Remove an installed package.
.It Ar query Ar package
Query the package database for information about a package.
.It Ar repo Ar subcommand Ar arguments
Manage package repositories.
.It Ar update
Update the local package database from repositories.
.It Ar upgrade
Upgrade all installed packages to their latest versions.
.It Ar search Ar keyword
Search for packages matching a keyword.
.It Ar info Ar package
Show detailed information about an installed package.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Install a package:
.Bd -literal
$ pkgctl install vim
.Ed
Remove a package:
.Bd -literal
$ pkgctl remove vim
.Ed
Search for packages:
.Bd -literal
$ pkgctl search editor
.Ed
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/pkgctl/repos.conf -compact
.It /var/db/pkgctl/
Directory containing the package database.
.It /var/db/pkgctl/pkglist.txt
List of installed packages in the format "name:version:description".
.It /etc/pkgctl/repos.conf
Configuration file containing repository URLs, one per line.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
pkg_add(8), pkg_delete(8), pkg_info(1), pkg_version(1)
.Sh HISTORY
pkgctl was first introduced in FreeBSD Mobile 13.0.
